ouch input via Origami’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"origami.Drag","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" patch, which wires its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"output ","type":"text"},{"code":"Position","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to the layer’s transform. The rendered view uses the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"centered 220×140 tan card, 888×1212 artboard, and full-bleed framing as the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"GitHub macOS runner evidence bound to this head.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview","role":"symbol"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView/mask(alignment:_:)":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview\/mask(alignment:_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView\/mask(alignment:_:)","abstract":[],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"mask"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Mask"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"alignment"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI9AlignmentV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Alignment"},{"kind":"text","text":", () -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Mask"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI4ViewP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"View"}],"title":"mask(alignment:_:)","kind":"symbol"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swami","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","abstract":[{"text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and native SwiftUI. One helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","title":"Swami"}}}